WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
- [Paulette] If you hate
somebody so bad in your heart

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.483
before you pass on,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.100
that hate will go to you.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.750
It will never go to the
person that you hate

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.173
and all the things that you-

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.650
Bombarded the person, people with,

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.500
are the things that you're
going to go through.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.953
That's how I feel, that-

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.693
Is the difference between love and hate.

00:00:34.758 --> 00:00:36.300
- [Interviewer] All right, Paulette.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.133
- [Paulette] Yes.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.260
- [Interviewer] Paulette,
where'd you grow up?

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.760
Where are you from originally?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.716
- [Paulette] Modesto, California up north.

00:00:42.716 --> 00:00:43.740
- [Interviewer] Modesto.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.280
And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.223
Did you had both of your
parents when you were young?

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.950
- I had my mother and my father.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.743
He passed away when I was
four and a half years old.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:06.260
My mom didn't pass away
until she was in her 70s

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.950
of Alzheimer's.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.900
- [Interviewer] How was your childhood?

00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:18.294
- At times, it was really good.

00:01:18.294 --> 00:01:21.623
And at times, it was super difficult,

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.823
because we weren't looked after real well.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.950
- [Interviewer] By your mom?

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:33.783
- Yeah.

00:01:35.391 --> 00:01:37.141
- [Interviewer] What was Mom doing?

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:42.773
- She was chasing an alcoholic boyfriend.

00:01:48.019 --> 00:01:51.429
So when somebody needed help

00:01:51.429 --> 00:01:52.573
in the family.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:58.950
She wasn't available

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:05.766
but I understand she grew
up knowing what she knew,

00:02:05.766 --> 00:02:07.452
how to be.

00:02:07.452 --> 00:02:08.440
And

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.973
same as I grew up, I grew
up not knowing anything,

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:19.563
but I had to teach myself a lot of things.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.140
- [Interviewer] How would
you describe your childhood?

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.290
- It's super difficult.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.913
I was perfect student.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.740
I loved school because home life was

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:36.963
very difficult.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.410
Some of the children
were getting in troubles,

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:43.320
going to

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.283
get locked up at different places.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.653
So I just blended in,

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.340
where I was seen and not heard

00:02:58.705 --> 00:03:00.500
- [Interviewer] What kind of
kid were you in high school?

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.333
- Pardon me?

00:03:01.333 --> 00:03:03.099
- [Interviewer] What kind of
kid were you in high school?

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:06.640
- I excelled in everything.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.473
I was...

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.193
the person that taught all the kids.

00:03:10.193 --> 00:03:12.890
A lot of their knowledge

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.073
from the books.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.480
I was straight A student

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:22.150
and...

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.673
I didn't have very many boyfriends.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:32.980
- [Interviewer] You're lonely?

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.160
- Yeah, and I have to-

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.215
Oh, gosh.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.048
I talked to-

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:37.140
Oh, wow.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.840
I have to say that's pretty,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.770
pretty fair to say.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:42.603
I-

00:03:43.909 --> 00:03:44.850
I wrote a poem

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.370
in the sixth grade.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.150
I think it was.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:50.911
And it was pertaining

00:03:50.911 --> 00:03:52.523
to the word, lonely.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.463
My lonely, empty heart.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.311
- [Interviewer] You went
on your own at what age?

00:04:02.311 --> 00:04:04.074
After high school?

00:04:04.074 --> 00:04:05.442
- Yes.

00:04:05.442 --> 00:04:06.275
(cheerful music)

00:04:06.275 --> 00:04:07.108
18 years old.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.980
I became responsible
to pay my mother's rent

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.620
where she lived on the house.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.140
She'd find the house and...

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.110
I paid the rent

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.480
so she could have that house

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.770
until she was ready to sell it

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.120
'cause she had bought a motor home,

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.993
a mobile home with her fiance.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.690
- [Interviewer] Do you have children?

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.293
- Yes, I have two sons.

00:04:45.777 --> 00:04:48.223
The oldest one is Frank Jr.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.340
He is...

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.393
40 years old.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.250
My youngest son

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.283
is Paul.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.273
And he's 30-

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.910
He's sometimes 37 and 38.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:07.823
He's about two to three
years younger than Frank.

00:05:09.055 --> 00:05:10.610
- [Interviewer] And you raised them?

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.593
- Oh, yes.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.333
I loved raising my children.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.240
They meant everything.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.723
I mean everything to me.

00:05:17.723 --> 00:05:19.100
- [Interviewer] Was that
the best time of your life?

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:19.933
- Yes.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.233
Yes.

00:05:22.233 --> 00:05:25.310
I chose like, if I were to be younger,

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:28.500
my favorite year would be 25 years old.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.100
That's when I had both my children

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.120
and I did everything that I could.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.523
I doted on them.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.200
I took them places.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:41.290
I drove them crazy at Christmas.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:44.520
I would take them to, it was
called Christmas Tree Lane.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.990
And I would take them like,

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.215
if they would go every single night,

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.400
twice a night,

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.540
I just love Christmas.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.040
There's something that's so...

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:58.960
happy for me.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.400
I don't know what it is.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.408
It's definitely for children.

00:06:02.408 --> 00:06:05.880
I don't have to have presence for them.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.033
Just decorations, you know?

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:11.205
And that makes me...

00:06:11.205 --> 00:06:14.870
(hand pounds on seat)

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:15.743
excited.

00:06:15.743 --> 00:06:17.590
- [Interviewer] It
brings back good memories

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:18.423
- Yeah.

00:06:18.423 --> 00:06:19.256
- [Interviewer] of your childhood.

00:06:19.256 --> 00:06:20.220
- Yes.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:21.053
Yeah.

00:06:21.053 --> 00:06:23.058
My favorite (laughs)

00:06:23.058 --> 00:06:27.060
is when my dad took me, Christmas playing,

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:30.363
let's say, one year. (laughs)

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.778
I got everything I ever wanted then.

00:06:34.778 --> 00:06:39.500
And
(vehicle rumbling)

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.993
It was incredible to me.

00:06:42.382 --> 00:06:43.910
I enjoyed it.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:45.720
- [Interviewer] But your dad passed away.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.530
- Yes.
- [Interviewer] When?

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.820
- I was four and a half years old.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:49.840
- [Interviewer] Four and a half.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.395
But do you remember your father?

00:06:51.395 --> 00:06:52.790
- Yes.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:54.193
Yes.

00:06:54.193 --> 00:06:56.513
He was a very good-looking man.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.240
If I had a picture of him,

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:03.083
one picture and he was a cook.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:09.200
He looks like Desi Arnaz

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.350
to me.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.790
So classy and...

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.760
handsome and...

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.483
steady, real steady person.

00:07:21.616 --> 00:07:23.500
- [Interviewer] So today,
you're living on skid row.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.680
- Yes, I am.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:25.993
- [Interviewer] How did that happen?

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.017
- I left my fiance

00:07:29.017 --> 00:07:30.723
of 13 years.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.180
That's the same amount of years

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.713
I was married to my husband.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:37.807
I left him, not because I didn't love him.

00:07:37.807 --> 00:07:39.310
It was because...

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:44.910
he became very rageful to the point,

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.610
I felt

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:50.060
and I told him that he was killing my soul

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:55.040
and I just couldn't take
the pressure that...

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.600
I felt.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:07:59.870
I loved my job.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.870
I was great at what I did,

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.423
but when I came home,

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.633
everything was messy.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:09.520
So...

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.635
it wasn't until I started working then.

00:08:12.635 --> 00:08:14.390
I really...

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:18.340
could tell the difference between Paulette

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.290
and...

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.680
that man's...

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.680
candy grill or whatever
you want to call it.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:28.193
I was a lot younger than him.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.640
I let him do anything he
wanted, anytime he wanted,

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.120
I never questioned anything.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.580
I never...

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.753
became suspicious.

00:08:42.603 --> 00:08:45.340
With my husband, I was pretty bad about...

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.170
not trusting.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.710
And so I let this man
just be so trustworthy.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:52.590
It was...

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.490
very comfortable for me

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:58.440
because I didn't have
to extra guess anything

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.183
and put extra things in my head.

00:09:01.939 --> 00:09:05.163
So when he was gone, I would just be me.

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:12.160
- [Interviewer] So there were trust issues

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.503
in both of those relationships?

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.563
- With my husband, yes.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.510
I trusted the second man

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.900
to the degree that...

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:29.210
I knew not to trust
him when he was rageful

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.983
and he became rageful daily.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:36.310
And I couldn't figure
out if it was his job.

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.980
If it was something about him personally

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:42.090
or he never wanted to get married.

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.300
And that was okay with me.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.240
I'm an open person.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.530
If that's...

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:48.883
the person I love.

00:09:50.695 --> 00:09:51.528
So,

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.160
I gave up asking the questions

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:00.030
and I felt like he had
this tremendous guilt

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.800
that he couldn't share with me.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.170
It was like,

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:04.003
almost-

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:07.543
It was pretty f'ed up.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:10.300
The look on his face.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:13.480
So I knew that he had something,

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:14.360
had to have something,

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:17.603
but I didn't spend a lot of
time trying to figure it out.

00:10:19.016 --> 00:10:21.430
- [Interviewer] That's
good, do you got out?

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.263
- Yeah.

00:10:22.263 --> 00:10:23.096
- [Interviewer] It's
good that you got out.

00:10:23.096 --> 00:10:23.929
- Yeah.

00:10:23.929 --> 00:10:26.810
Because he did get me in the garage, once.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.193
I had a neck surgery,

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.280
got a plate in my neck

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.360
and he got me up in the garage

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.250
and picked me up by my neck.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.170
And the neighbor man came driving by

00:10:40.615 --> 00:10:43.280
and immediately came over

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:47.503
and he dropped me like quick.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.873
- [Interviewer] And you
ended up homeless, how?

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:55.610
- [Paulette] When I left that man,

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.830
I had really good credit

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.247
and I don't know why.

00:11:00.247 --> 00:11:02.310
I didn't think to...

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.523
use my money.

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:14.585
To get my own place or my own independence

00:11:14.585 --> 00:11:16.890
or anything like that.

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:18.963
As it turns out,

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:25.230
I feel that it was the best
thing that ever happened.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:27.170
My choice,

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:31.453
number one, I didn't put my
children through terrific hell.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:36.430
They did not know my whereabouts.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:39.560
My youngest son found me probably a yea-

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:44.560
Not about 8 months ago through
a Christian people group.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:48.790
And he asked that they
search for me and they did.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.503
And they found me in six months.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.140
So I didn't want my children

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:56.120
to have to hear all these stories

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:59.723
and secondhand things
that was going on with me.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:03.220
So I felt it best that I just...

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:06.140
cut it off.

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:09.190
And I found out my youngest
son had been looking for me,

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:11.743
no matter what, no matter what.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:16.810
For quite a few years.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:17.710
And...

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.860
because I am the mother

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.343
that raised him.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.847
I believe that he also felt

00:12:30.847 --> 00:12:35.120
that this mother that
was out here on skid row

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:38.203
could still be quite sufficient.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.123
He's told me,

00:12:45.123 --> 00:12:47.430
I don't know how many times
that he's proud of me.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:55.750
He's told me some cute
little stories about...

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:02.400
some things I shared with
him about him and myself

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:04.803
and possibly his older brother,

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:07.633
spiritual thing.

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:13.720
And the way he told me these
stories were just like,

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:16.520
I hear them here, (chuckles)

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.160
today.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.253
And I know that-

00:13:24.449 --> 00:13:29.449
That he's here in spirit, of course.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:32.083
Mind, soul, body, and
spirit, I don't know.

00:13:34.846 --> 00:13:37.013
(exhales)

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.063
Being proud.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:46.975
I've changed a lot.

00:13:46.975 --> 00:13:47.983
I'm very-

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:53.600
I say anything I want
just about to anybody.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.733
I pray a lot on that.

00:13:59.577 --> 00:14:04.203
Certain things that people
say and have done against me.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.030
I have s-

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:10.530
With my spirit getting very stern

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.740
about my feelings of...

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.043
the process that they must go through.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.530
Like, here's for instance,

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:24.093
if you hate somebody so bad in your heart,

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.483
before you pass on,

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:31.100
that hate will go to you.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:35.600
It will never go to the
person that you hate

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.173
and all the things that you-

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:42.650
Bombarded the person, people with,

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:45.500
are the things that you're
going to go through.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:46.953
That's how I feel that-

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.713
Is the difference between love and hate.

00:14:55.728 --> 00:14:57.810
- [Interviewer] Are drugs
a part of your life?

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:01.180
- Yes, I did do crack cocaine,

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:02.083
in the beginning.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:04.860
- [Interviewer] In the beginning of?

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:07.823
- Of my usage, I used for about,

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:10.680
14 years.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:11.670
And...

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:18.304
I don't feel that I used
as many people out there

00:15:18.304 --> 00:15:20.940
that are on drugs.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.270
In the beginning, I did,
I went way overboard,

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.870
but I learned how to function

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.898
and how to...

00:15:27.898 --> 00:15:28.930
think

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.860
and still say prayers

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.383
because no matter what.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:40.313
The God of my understanding tells me,

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.520
I take you as you are.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.753
I will change the things
that I need to change in you.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:49.565
Not them, their-

00:15:49.565 --> 00:15:51.850
- [Interviewer] This
began, the drug use began,

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.340
during your second relationship?

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.300
- After.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.950
In...

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:56.850
2005.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.783
- [Interviewer] So when
you became homeless?

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:03.150
- I started working in the streets.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.283
I mean, everything.

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:06.653
I was a suburbian.

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:10.685
Learning how to grow up in s-

00:16:10.685 --> 00:16:12.710
gangster life.

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:15.130
'Cause these are gangsters out here.

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:16.380
They're hell-raisers.

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:17.213
They're...

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:19.043
brutal.

00:16:20.692 --> 00:16:22.410
- [Interviewer] Did you have
bad things happen to you here?

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.690
- Oh, yes.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:25.410
A lot of things.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:28.507
And finally, today, I just
look at them and I say,

00:16:28.507 --> 00:16:32.350
"If you're going to like
a homie hostage, kill me,

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:34.397
or whatever you think you want to do.

00:16:34.397 --> 00:16:35.330
Go ahead,

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:37.600
'cause you're going to
hell no matter what,

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:38.433
you will go to hell.

00:16:38.433 --> 00:16:42.610
I don't pay the price and I'm
going to walk away from you."

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.433
And I end up walking away.

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:47.839
It's the darndest thing because...

00:16:47.839 --> 00:16:52.000
I had some guy stick me in
a car and hold me hostage.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.610
And nobody could get in
this car, even though,

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.663
it was unlocked,

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:59.670
it was unlocked and...

00:17:00.805 --> 00:17:04.490
it is because of the power
of prayer that I acknowledge

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:07.720
that puts people at bay.

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:08.553
They can-

00:17:08.553 --> 00:17:10.250
I don't care what they think.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.127
I hear women tell me,

00:17:11.127 --> 00:17:13.720
"They're going to whip
my ass and take my shit."

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:14.760
And go ahead,

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.087
if they think they can,

00:17:16.087 --> 00:17:18.120
'cause my spiritual

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:21.070
persona

00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:25.210
tells me, they can't get
that far from me anymore.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:26.800
They can't swing at me.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:27.860
They can't.

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.150
They could do other weird stuff, maybe,

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.810
that I don't know how to...

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:36.500
Change.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:38.950
But I've learned by...

00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:43.210
biting my way through.

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:48.100
I actually am my own soldier basically,

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:48.933
to...

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:52.373
fight.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.063
For what I represent.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:01.830
- [Interviewer] Have you been
raped or anything like that?

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:02.663
- Yep.

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:05.123
- [Interviewer] Pretty much every woman

00:18:05.123 --> 00:18:07.513
that's down here has encountered that.

00:18:09.814 --> 00:18:10.964
And where do you sleep?

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:13.960
- I sleep

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:15.390
in a tent.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:17.760
I am changing where I live today

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.830
because there's been some...

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:29.480
strong things that have
taken place between me

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:33.390
and it was supposed to be one person,

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:35.883
but it turned out to be
the entire neighborhood.

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:41.880
So I'm not going to be
participating in negativity.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:42.713
It's just not my style.

00:18:42.713 --> 00:18:44.220
- [Interviewer] (laughs) It's over here.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.140
- It's not my style.

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.650
- [Interviewer] Yeah, well, good luck.

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:47.700
I was waiting that here.

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:48.533
- I do.

00:18:48.533 --> 00:18:50.170
I just stay away.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.003
And...

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.870
I say to the person,

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:57.160
what I think is going on

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:59.570
and (laughs) I don't care.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.240
My spirit is so strong.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.580
I am

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.200
so precise.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:07.193
It's incredible, it's totally-

00:19:07.193 --> 00:19:08.100
- [Interviewer] You're investing yourself

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:10.033
'cause you're in the heart of-

00:19:10.033 --> 00:19:11.420
- I've had to grow up here

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:14.210
and learn the true life

00:19:16.173 --> 00:19:19.843
as uncomfortable as it
may make others feel.

00:19:21.097 --> 00:19:25.320
I care about myself
and I love myself today

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.384
because of anything and everything

00:19:28.384 --> 00:19:30.930
that took place in my past.

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:32.762
It's made me

00:19:32.762 --> 00:19:33.933
who I am.

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:35.950
And I love that.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.640
A lot of people don't like that.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:38.550
- [Interviewer] Are you happy, today?

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:39.513
- Yes.

00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:43.967
On the most part, I've
had to really say, "Yes."

00:19:45.595 --> 00:19:50.595
It's been a hard fight,
but it's also been,

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:53.550
I've had to question a lot of things.

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:56.880
And when I talked to my
son on the phone, I knew.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:57.803
I knew.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:04.040
A lot of things were
going to get worked out.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.310
- [Interviewer] Have your sons come to,

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:07.053
try to take you out of here?

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:09.193
- He asked me if I-

00:20:10.123 --> 00:20:13.000
if I wanna (laughs)

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.380
He asked me if I wanted to

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:18.210
go to a program and recover,

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:21.170
and I said, "No, I'm not ready."

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.970
And now, today, I can tell you,

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.903
I know what he was talking about.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:27.820
I've had to...

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.030
Reprogram

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.020
a lot of

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:39.090
structure around me

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:42.900
so that I could break through

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:43.760
and...

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:51.208
so I can be me.

00:20:51.208 --> 00:20:53.370
- [Interviewer] Are you
still using drugs today?

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:54.230
- Barely.

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.400
Yes, I use...

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.360
meth.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:00.260
I quit...

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:04.000
crack because this man,

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.180
a friend of mine started using it

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.350
and it wasn't correct,

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:12.100
the way I knew crack was supposed to be.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:15.483
And like I couldn't get the
inhalation and the smoke.

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:18.856
It was like sucking, like (inhaling)

00:21:18.856 --> 00:21:22.690
without getting anything,
not even barely any air.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:25.500
And I quit instantly.

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:28.250
It was the best thing, actually
that happened, I think.

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:32.503
I kinda missed the feelings
that I used to get.

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:34.483
I used to actually,

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:39.750
I could hear angels constantly.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:41.040
And I know I wasn't hallucinating

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:43.620
because when I would stop,

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:45.270
unlike when I went to jail and stuff,

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:47.130
I could still hear them.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:48.440
- [Interviewer] This was on crack.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.273
- Yeah.

00:21:49.273 --> 00:21:50.763
And then off of crack,

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.393
I could still hear them.

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:56.133
And...

00:21:59.344 --> 00:22:03.150
it's not that they're seeing or anything.

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:05.920
It's like one voice talks to me,

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:07.563
but several at the same time.

00:22:13.208 --> 00:22:15.960
- [Interviewer] How do
you support yourself now?

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:19.240
- I'm on GR food stamps.

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:24.240
And I barely ever spend
my food stamps on drugs.

00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:25.823
I mean, barely.

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:32.523
Probably did 10 bucks all of six months.

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:37.590
And I have worked the streets.

00:22:37.590 --> 00:22:39.070
I have calmed down on that

00:22:39.070 --> 00:22:40.720
because...

00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:45.640
I don't care for the street owners

00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:46.753
of each street.

00:22:48.140 --> 00:22:50.600
They bombard me.

00:22:50.600 --> 00:22:55.240
They try to get one over on
me and they try to use me.

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:56.730
And I don't play that game.

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:58.750
I stay away from that territory.

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:01.030
It's just, you know, used to be mine.

00:23:01.030 --> 00:23:03.960
I used to have (swoosh), like that

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:05.940
because of the power of prayer.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:06.773
But now,

00:23:09.890 --> 00:23:11.550
I get dates every now and then,

00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:13.970
just men driving in vehicles,

00:23:13.970 --> 00:23:15.270
wherever I'm walking,

00:23:15.270 --> 00:23:17.010
it doesn't (chuckles)

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:17.843
make a difference.

00:23:17.843 --> 00:23:20.730
You know, it doesn't have to be every day.

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.570
And I use the money for things

00:23:22.570 --> 00:23:24.163
that I want or need.

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:32.507
It's usually cigarettes or food

00:23:32.507 --> 00:23:33.540
or

00:23:34.905 --> 00:23:36.490
clothing

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:37.323
or

00:23:38.220 --> 00:23:39.903
this time I want a radio.

00:23:39.903 --> 00:23:43.060
- [Interviewer] Crystal
meth, you'll pay for how?

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:46.793
- Sometimes, the men that I know have it,

00:23:47.670 --> 00:23:49.116
want to have a favor,

00:23:49.116 --> 00:23:51.973
so they share with me,
some do, some don't.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:59.240
Sometimes, there's just guys that I meet

00:23:59.240 --> 00:24:00.650
and I'm very specific with them

00:24:00.650 --> 00:24:03.230
that I'm not there to give pleasure.

00:24:03.230 --> 00:24:06.520
I just want to get high and
that they don't want that.

00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:08.760
And then, I turn them down.

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:09.830
Not a lot of guys,

00:24:09.830 --> 00:24:10.963
I trust really.

00:24:12.650 --> 00:24:16.610
They tend to get sneaky on you, you know.

00:24:16.610 --> 00:24:18.910
Not all, but a lot of them.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:20.853
- [Interviewer] And Paulette,

00:24:20.853 --> 00:24:22.633
what's the most important
lesson you've learned?

00:24:29.630 --> 00:24:31.553
- To trust in myself,

00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:34.000
trust in

00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:38.733
the path that I am supposed to be in.

00:24:41.210 --> 00:24:43.970
Trust in my thought process

00:24:44.810 --> 00:24:45.800
and...

00:24:49.238 --> 00:24:51.390
(sniffs)

00:24:51.390 --> 00:24:56.390
don't trust in the hellions. (chuckles)

00:24:58.020 --> 00:24:59.680
That's just people that...

00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:05.020
they think that they're
getting up on over on me

00:25:05.020 --> 00:25:08.260
and I haven't pegged pretty much,

00:25:08.260 --> 00:25:10.663
before they can even start their engines.

00:25:12.920 --> 00:25:16.260
I sometimes get scared

00:25:16.260 --> 00:25:18.073
'cause sometimes I think I'm,

00:25:19.270 --> 00:25:20.103
you know,

00:25:20.103 --> 00:25:22.400
on the wrong path, but I
know I'm on the right path.

00:25:22.400 --> 00:25:23.233
I feel it.

00:25:23.233 --> 00:25:25.680
I feel it super strong.

00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:30.680
Off and on, it's days that I
feel so sad and distraught.

00:25:30.846 --> 00:25:33.677
And then, there's days that I feel like,

00:25:33.677 --> 00:25:34.807
"We are moving."

00:25:34.807 --> 00:25:36.864
"We are chewing this thing."

00:25:36.864 --> 00:25:38.126
Yeah.

00:25:38.126 --> 00:25:39.363
It's wonderful.

00:25:40.757 --> 00:25:41.635
- [Interviewer] All right, Paulette.

00:25:41.635 --> 00:25:43.012
Well, thank you so much
for sharing your story.

00:25:43.012 --> 00:25:43.981
- Thank you.

00:25:43.981 --> 00:25:46.230
- [Interviewer] And I wish you
the best of luck out there.

00:25:46.230 --> 00:25:47.380
- Oh, it's gonna be- (chuckles)

00:25:47.380 --> 00:25:48.640
- [Interviewer] Be careful.

00:25:48.640 --> 00:25:50.013
- Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:53.060
- [Interviewer] It's dangerous
for a woman out there, right?

00:25:53.060 --> 00:25:53.893
- [Paulette] Huh?

00:25:53.893 --> 00:25:54.860
- [Interviewer] It's dangerous
for a woman out there.

00:25:54.860 --> 00:25:56.060
- [Paulette] Oh, I know.

00:25:58.041 --> 00:26:00.270
(sniffs and laughs)

00:26:00.270 --> 00:26:01.189
- [Interviewer] Thank you.

00:26:01.189 --> 00:26:03.106
- [Paulette] Thank you.

